      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "To actively disrupt these passive readings, you need to introduce countermeasures that interfere with the physical signals the chair is detecting. Wearing clothing made of highly insulating, multi-layered, or conductive materials could potentially disrupt heat signature readings and alter skin conductivity. Additionally, consciously shifting your weight or posture in a randomized, non-predictable manner can scramble the pressure point data the sensors are trying to log. You are essentially creating noise in the data stream, making the readings meaningless to any system.",
